opencode is an open source terminal coding agent.  It provides an
interactive and non-interactive CLI for working with code through
supported language models, including OpenAI, Anthropic, Google,
DeepSeek, and others via OpenRouter.

Key features:

- Interactive and non-interactive CLI modes
- Supports 20+ AI providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, DeepSeek, Groq, etc.)
- Built-in tools for file search (glob), content search (grep), file
  reading/editing/writing, shell execution, and web fetching
- Customizable agents and subagents
- Session management with compaction and summaries
- Configurable via opencode.json (providers, models, permissions)

This OpenBSD port targets the core CLI.  Plugin support and
self-upgrade are disabled.  Startup time is approximately 20
seconds due to TypeScript transpilation at runtime.
